  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway by which Jerantinine B may influence U373 MG cells, through the targeting of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and other proteins. This relationship is supported by the shared target of Jerantinine B with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is then targeted by multiple compounds, including Rhetsinine and Pseudopterosin Q. These findings indicate that Jerantinine B may act through a common intermediate, Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, to exert its effects on U373 MG. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism by which Jerantinine B interacts with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway highlights the complexity of the interaction network, and further studies would be needed to determine the precise role of each component in the overall effect on U373 MG.",
